new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6aedd7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deploy.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy
+
+Fizzy is set up to run on a single Linux server with Docker and SQLite.
+Kamal builds the image, runs the app (and background jobs) in one container,
+and terminates SSL at the proxy.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed and ports 80 and 443 open
+- SSH access to that server
+- A hostname with DNS pointing at the server
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Fork this repository.
+2. In `config/deploy.yml`, set:
+   - `servers.web` to your server
+   - `proxy.host` and `APP_HOST` to your hostname
+   - `SMTP_ADDRESS` / `SMTP_USERNAME` / `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` to your mail server
+3. In `.kamal/secrets`, provide `SECRET_KEY_BASE` (from `bin/rails secret`) and `SMTP_PASSWORD`.
+4. Run:
+
+```sh
+kamal setup
+```
+
+Fizzy will be at `https://your-host`. SQLite and uploaded files live in the
+`fizzy_storage` Docker volume, so they survive the next `kamal deploy`.
+Jobs run on the box inside the web container (Solid Queue in Puma).
